{
  "$comment": [
    "The release evidence gate's configuration, read at the release commit by scripts/dev/release_evidence.py",
    "(vendored from the development kit; its docs/ci-evidence.md is the contract, docs/releasing.md says how the",
    "release uses it). .github/test_ci_evidence.py holds this file to ci.yml and release.yml.",
    "Native sandbox coverage includes the Windows customer registration and approved-acquisition refusal."
  ],
  "schema": 2,
  "repository": "Judgment-Pack/judgment-pack-gateway",
  "branch": "main",
  "max_age_hours": 48,
  "inputs": [
    ".dockerignore",
    ".github/workflows/release.yml",
    ".goreleaser.yml",
    "Dockerfile",
    "adapters/agreement/agreement_test.go",
    "adapters/go.mod",
    "adapters/go.sum",
    "build/mkhomes.go",
    "build/setcap.go",
    "catalog/postgres.json",
    "go/go.mod",
    "jpdev.json",
    "plugins/activepieces/judgment-pack/package-lock.json",
    "plugins/n8n-nodes-judgment-pack/package-lock.json",
    "scripts/checks/image-root-unwritable.sh",
    "scripts/checks/witness-scenario.sh",
    "scripts/dev/changed_checks.py",
    "scripts/dev/check.sh",
    "testdata/attachments/schema-requirements.txt",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/commonmark/go.mod",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/commonmark/go.sum",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/metaschema/go.mod",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/metaschema/go.sum",
    "verify-ts/package-lock.json"
  ],
  "fresh_at_release": [
    "tag grammar, tag names the commit, commit on main",
    "release notes",
    "production environment reviewer",
    "third-party notices with the release toolchain",
    "packaging, packaged checksums, archive contents",
    "native archive runs: linux amd64 and arm64, macOS arm64, Windows amd64",
    "tag still names the commit, no release under the tag",
    "attestation",
    "draft identity",
    "production approval",
    "published asset digests"
  ],
  "profiles": {
    "check": {
      "$comment": [
        "The check job: the Go release.yml names, Node and Python as dev.json names them, Docker as the image has it.",
        "The release job sets the same three up with the same actions and resolves them here (release-runner)."
      ],
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Linux",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "release-runner",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ],
        "node": [
          "node",
          "--version"
        ],
        "python": [
          "python3",
          "--version"
        ],
        "docker": [
          "docker",
          "--version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 linux/amd64"
      }
    },
    "go-linux": {
      "$comment": "The Linux leg of the go matrix, on the release job's platform: resolved there too (release-runner).",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Linux",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "release-runner",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 linux/amd64"
      }
    },
    "go-macos": {
      "$comment": "The macOS leg: another OS and architecture than the release job's, so held to its pin.",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "macOS",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "ARM64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 darwin/arm64"
      }
    },
    "go-windows": {
      "$comment": "The Windows leg: another OS than the release job's, so held to its pin.",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Windows",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 windows/amd64"
      }
    }
  },
  "workflows": {
    "ci": {
      "$comment": [
        "Only a push to main is evidence: ci.yml has no dispatch, so the fresh route is a re-run of all jobs of main's run.",
        "Every job and every matrix leg is required; none is skipped on main. The go legs include native adapter sandbox boundary tests and run the workflow's own steps,",
        "not dev.json's, so their checks are none: the job's success is the API's, and the evidence adds the leg's",
        "platform and toolchain. The check job runs every dev.json check and setup step."
      ],
      "path": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
      "name": "CI",
      "events": [
        "push"
      ],
      "jobs": {
        "check": {
          "name": "check",
          "job_id": "check",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "check",
          "checks": "all",
          "optional_skips": [],
          "setup": true
        },
        "go-ubuntu-latest": {
          "name": "ubuntu-latest \u00b7 Go 1.26",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-linux",
          "checks": []
        },
        "go-macos-latest": {
          "name": "macos-latest \u00b7 Go 1.26",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "macos-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-macos",
          "checks": []
        },
        "go-windows-latest": {
          "name": "windows-latest \u00b7 Go 1.26",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "windows-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-windows",
          "checks": []
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "tag": {
    "prerelease": true
  }
}
